# Keeps the top-level Dockerfile build (Railway deploy image) from sending the
# whole repo as build context to the daemon — that Dockerfile only COPYs
# pyproject.toml/uv.lock*/README.md/src/case_study/.env.example, so nothing
# else here is ever needed inside the image.
#
# Real bug found 2026-08-30: an earlier version of this file also excluded
# `case_study/` and `*.md`, which broke THIS build (`COPY case_study/
# ./case_study/` and `COPY ... README.md ./` both failed with "not found") —
# confirmed failing on `main`'s own `docker.yml` CI run after that version
# merged. `.dockerignore` at the repo root applies to every Docker build
# using this context (both this Dockerfile and `docker/sandbox/Dockerfile`),
# so it must only exclude what NEITHER build needs. The sandbox image's own
# narrower, safe-for-it-but-not-for-this-one exclusions
# (`case_study/`) live in `docker/sandbox/Dockerfile.dockerignore` instead —
# Docker resolves a per-Dockerfile ignore file named
# `<path-to-dockerfile-relative-to-context>.dockerignore` automatically.

.git/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
frontend/
.claude/
docs/
tests/
.env
.env.local
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
